		{"id":"914157f4c680e1b2","x":500,"y":-440,"width":652,"height":1120,"type":"text","text":"```json\n# ontology_relations\n{\n  \"id\": \"string\",                       // unique relation ID\n  \"concept_ref\": {\n    \"concept_id\": \"string\",\n    \"concept_name\": \"string\",\n    \"kind\": \"entity | metric | dimension | dq_rule | process\",\n    \"domain\": \"string\"\n  },\n\n  \"expression_ref\": {\n    \"expression_id\": \"string\",          // MUST come from ontology_concepts\n    \"expression_name\": \"string\",\n    \"logic_type\": \n      \"identity | computation | derivation | validation | aggregation\",\n    \"version\": \"v1\"\n  },\n\n  \"input_spec\": {\n    \"input_role\": \"string\",             // e.g., actual_amount\n    \"input_kind\": \n      \"entity | metric | dimension | attribute\",\n\n    \"business_field\": {\n      \"field_name\": \"string\",           // business-level name\n      \"field_type\": \"string\",           // numeric, date, enum, etc.\n      \"description\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n\n  \"usage\": {\n    \"required_for\": \n      \"computation | validation | aggregation | reporting\",\n    \"is_mandatory\": true\n  },\n\n  \"confidence_score\": 0.0,\n  \"status\": \"proposed | confirmed | rejected\",\n  \"inferred_by\": \"llm | heuristic | user\",\n\n  \"embedding_input\": \"rich description combining concept + expression + field\",\n  \"embedding_vector\": [],\n\n  \"created_at\": { \"$date\": \"timestamp\" },\n  \"updated_at\": { \"$date\": \"timestamp\" }\n}\n \n```"},
		{"id":"5f0f8196e59d8fbb","x":500,"y":-5680,"width":854,"height":1600,"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"02c2eac9-2ae9-4b3c-ba2d-2d7daf4a33ae\",\n  \"concept_id\": \"ent_trial_balance\",\n  \"relation_id\": \"b1e1c3f4-5f8e-4c9b-8c1e-3f8e1c3f4b8e\",\n  \"kind\": \"entity\",\n  \"expression\": \"\",\n  \"data_object_id\": [\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadta\": [\n      {\n\t      \"column_id\": \"\",\n\t      \"column_name\": \"\",\n\t      \"description\": \"\",\n\t  },\n\t  {\n\t\t  \"column_id\": \"\",\n\t      \"column_name\": \"\",\n\t      \"description\": \"\",\n\t  }\n      ],\n    },\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadta\": [\n      {\n\t      \"column_id\": \"\",\n\t      \"column_name\": \"\",\n\t      \"description\": \"\",\n\t  },\n\t  {\n\t\t  \"column_id\": \"\",\n\t      \"column_name\": \"\",\n\t      \"description\": \"\",\n\t  }\n      ],\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"confidence_score\": 0.85,\n  \"status\": \"active\",\n  \"inferred_by\": \"llm\",\n  \"embedding_input\": \"The unique identifier for the trial balance report in financial accounting serves as a critical string representation that ensures accounting integrity by validating that total debits equal total credits for a specific reporting period. This identifier, known as event_id, tracks specific financial transaction events and is linked to the account_number, which uniquely identifies financial accounts within the trial balance reporting framework. Both identifiers play essential roles in gl_accounting workflows and financial reporting processes, maintaining relationships with the General Ledger to uphold the accuracy and reliability of financial data across the finance domain.\",\n  \"embedding_vector\": [],\n    \"created_at\": {\n    \"$date\": \"2025-12-17T12:14:20.346Z\"\n  },\n  \"updated_at\": {\n    \"$date\": \"2025-12-17T12:14:20.346Z\"\n  }\n}\n```"},
		{"id":"1a8de1dbda2e3ccc","x":2040,"y":-5680,"width":840,"height":1660,"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"id\": \"d3c8f5e2-4c3b-4c8e-8b8f-4e1c5e8c8b5e\",\n  \"concept_id\": \"ent_chart_of_accounts\",\n  \"kind\": \"entity\",\n  \"business_fields\": [\n    {\n      \"field_id\": \"a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7g8h-9i0j-k1l2m3n4o5p6\",\n      \"field_name\": \"account_id\",\n      \"field_type\": \"string\",\n      \"required_for\": \"validation\",\n      \"description\": \"Unique identifier for each account in the chart.\",\n      \"embedding_input\": \"The field 'account_id' is a string type that serves as a unique identifier for each account in the Chart of Accounts. This field is crucial for validation purposes, ensuring that each account can be distinctly recognized and referenced in financial transactions. It supports the integrity of the accounting system by preventing duplication and confusion among accounts. In FP&A and GL workflows, this identifier is used to link transactions to specific accounts, facilitating accurate reporting and analysis.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"field_id\": \"b1c2d3e4-f5g6-h7i8-j9k0-l1m2n3o4p5q6\",\n      \"field_name\": \"account_name\",\n      \"field_type\": \"string\",\n      \"required_for\": \"reporting\",\n      \"description\": \"Descriptive name of the financial account.\",\n      \"embedding_input\": \"The 'account_name' field is a string type that provides a descriptive name for each financial account in the Chart of Accounts. This field is essential for reporting purposes, as it allows users to easily identify and understand the nature of each account. In FP&A and GL workflows, account names are used in financial statements and reports, making it easier for stakeholders to interpret financial data. The clarity provided by this field enhances communication and understanding of financial activities.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"field_id\": \"c1d2e3f4-g5h6-i7j8-k9l0-m1n2o3p4q5r6\",\n      \"field_name\": \"account_type\",\n      \"field_type\": \"enum\",\n      \"required_for\": \"classification\",\n      \"description\": \"Type of account (e.g., asset, liability, equity, revenue, expense).\",\n      \"embedding_input\": \"The 'account_type' field is an enum type that categorizes each account into predefined types such as asset, liability, equity, revenue, or expense. This classification is vital for financial reporting and analysis, as it helps in organizing accounts into meaningful groups. In FP&A and GL workflows, understanding account types is crucial for preparing financial statements and conducting variance analysis. This field supports the overall structure of the Chart of Accounts by ensuring that accounts are appropriately categorized.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"field_id\": \"d1e2f3g4-h5i6-j7k8-l9m0-n1o2p3q4r5s6\",\n      \"field_name\": \"account_code\",\n      \"field_type\": \"string\",\n      \"required_for\": \"validation\",\n      \"description\": \"Numeric or alphanumeric code assigned to the account.\",\n      \"embedding_input\": \"The 'account_code' field is a string type that represents a numeric or alphanumeric code assigned to each account in the Chart of Accounts. This code is used for validation purposes, ensuring that transactions are recorded against the correct accounts. In FP&A and GL workflows, account codes facilitate the efficient processing of financial data and help in maintaining consistency across financial records. This field is integral to the structure of the Chart of Accounts, allowing for quick identification and retrieval of account information.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"field_id\": \"e1f2g3h4-i5j6-k7l8-m9n0-o1p2q3r4s5t6\",\n      \"field_name\": \"parent_account_id\",\n      \"field_type\": \"string\",\n      \"required_for\": \"aggregation\",\n      \"description\": \"Identifier for the parent account in a hierarchical structure.\",\n      \"embedding_input\": \"The 'parent_account_id' field is a string type that identifies the parent account in a hierarchical structure of the Chart of Accounts. This field is important for aggregation purposes, allowing for the consolidation of financial data at different levels of the account hierarchy. In FP&A and GL workflows, it supports the creation of summarized financial reports and helps in understanding the relationships between accounts. This hierarchical structure enhances the usability of the Chart of Accounts by providing a clear view of account relationships.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"domain\": \"gl_accounting\",\n  \"concept_expression\": null,\n  \"embedding_input\": \"The concept 'Chart of Accounts' (ID: ent_chart_of_accounts) is an entity within the domain of GL Accounting. It represents a structured listing of financial accounts that classifies all financial activity into consistent, reportable categories, forming the backbone of financial reporting and analysis. The Chart of Accounts is essential for organizing financial data, ensuring that transactions are recorded accurately and can be reported effectively. The detailed context highlights its role in providing a framework for financial reporting, enabling stakeholders to analyze financial performance. The business fields associated with this concept include 'account_id', 'account_name', 'account_type', 'account_code', and 'parent_account_id', each serving specific purposes such as validation, reporting, classification, and aggregation. Together, these fields support the overall functionality of the Chart of Accounts, ensuring that financial data is structured, accessible, and meaningful for analysis and reporting.\",\n  \"created_at\": {\n    \"$date\": \"2025-12-17T12:47:31.147Z\"\n  },\n  \"embedding_vector\": []\n  }\n```\n"},
		{"id":"7afc340ddc001483","x":1460,"y":-10280,"width":400,"height":1130,"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\n  \"_id\": {\n    \"$oid\": \"6942af350c0862bc8a5689c1\"\n  },\n  \"id\": \"6e76bc47-282e-4d19-bac2-54f284afc0da\",\n  \"concept_id\": \"ent_chart_of_accounts\",\n  \"relation_id\": \"b3f4c2e1-5e3b-4c8e-8b8f-4e1c5e8c8b5e\",\n  \"kind\": \"entity\",\n  \"expression\": \"\",\n  \"data_object_id\": [\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"f1e5c3b1-1e6e-4c8e-8b8f-4e1c5e8c8b5e\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"account_id\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadata\": [\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"b752f0a08ba4f281660feb86afaf567b\",\n          \"column_name\": \"account_number\",\n          \"description\": \"The account_number serves as a unique identifier for financial accounts, aligning with the need for classifying financial activities in the Chart of Accounts for accurate reporting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"d594233dfb7e4775de6bb7c326d3818e\",\n          \"column_name\": \"account_type\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'account_type' column classifies financial accounts, aligning with the search query's focus on organizing financial data within the Chart of Accounts for accurate reporting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"2345542334b425a606deab60d9197543\",\n          \"column_name\": \"member_name\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'member_name' column represents financial account names used for classification and reporting, aligning with the need for unique identifiers in the Chart of Accounts.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"37dfea235d8b0fdb4e98aac530a8204f\",\n          \"column_name\": \"dim\",\n          \"description\": \"The column categorizes financial accounts within the Chart of Accounts hierarchy, aligning with the need for unique identifiers in GL Accounting for accurate financial reporting.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"f2e5c3b1-1e6e-4c8e-8b8f-4e1c5e8c8b5e\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"account_name\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadata\": [\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"7b7e54c7a58599e3bd2aee95a41e5a46\",\n          \"column_name\": \"account_description\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'account_description' column directly aligns with the search query's focus on the descriptive name of financial accounts, essential for organizing and classifying financial activities in the General Ledger.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"2345542334b425a606deab60d9197543\",\n          \"column_name\": \"member_name\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'member_name' column represents the name of financial accounts, aligning with the need for descriptive account names in the Chart of Accounts for financial reporting and analysis.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"d594233dfb7e4775de6bb7c326d3818e\",\n          \"column_name\": \"account_type\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'account_type' column categorizes financial accounts, aligning with the need for organizing and classifying accounts in the Chart of Accounts for accurate financial reporting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"37dfea235d8b0fdb4e98aac530a8204f\",\n          \"column_name\": \"dim\",\n          \"description\": \"The column categorizes financial accounts within the Chart of Accounts, aligning with the need for organizing and classifying financial activities in GL Accounting.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"f3e5c3b1-1e6e-4c8e-8b8f-4e1c5e8c8b5e\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"account_type\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadata\": [\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"d594233dfb7e4775de6bb7c326d3818e\",\n          \"column_name\": \"account_type\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'account_type' column categorizes financial accounts into classifications like asset, liability, and equity, aligning directly with the search query's focus on financial account types in GL Accounting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"37dfea235d8b0fdb4e98aac530a8204f\",\n          \"column_name\": \"dim\",\n          \"description\": \"This column categorizes financial accounts into types such as asset, liability, equity, revenue, or expense, aligning directly with the search query's focus on financial account classification in GL Accounting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"f20c0b1e4e6a7d84316587c74c10fc6e\",\n          \"column_name\": \"type\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'type' column categorizes financial entries, aligning with the search query's focus on classifying financial accounts in GL Accounting.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"f4e5c3b1-1e6e-4c8e-8b8f-4e1c5e8c8b5e\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"parent_account_id\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadata\": [\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"17bb847eda58f164970c690e4f1ba7a1\",\n          \"column_name\": \"parent_name\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'parent_name' column identifies the parent account in the Chart of Accounts hierarchy, aligning with the need for organizing financial data in GL Accounting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"37dfea235d8b0fdb4e98aac530a8204f\",\n          \"column_name\": \"dim\",\n          \"description\": \"The column categorizes financial accounts within a hierarchy, aligning with the search query's focus on organizing financial data in the Chart of Accounts.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"d594233dfb7e4775de6bb7c326d3818e\",\n          \"column_name\": \"account_type\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'account_type' column categorizes financial accounts, which supports the organization and classification of accounts in the Chart of Accounts, aligning with the search query's focus on financial data structuring.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"f5e5c3b1-1e6e-4c8e-8b8f-4e1c5e8c8b5e\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"account_status\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadata\": [\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"d594233dfb7e4775de6bb7c326d3818e\",\n          \"column_name\": \"account_type\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'account_type' column classifies financial accounts, aligning with the search query's focus on the status of accounts in GL Accounting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"37dfea235d8b0fdb4e98aac530a8204f\",\n          \"column_name\": \"dim\",\n          \"description\": \"This column categorizes financial accounts, which aligns with the search query's focus on the status of accounts in GL Accounting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"f20c0b1e4e6a7d84316587c74c10fc6e\",\n          \"column_name\": \"type\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'type' column categorizes financial entries, which aligns with the need to classify accounts as active or inactive in financial reporting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"b1c15997a87fb977856f9da12aa840bd\",\n          \"column_name\": \"event\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'event' column captures financial events related to the trial balance, which can indicate the status of accounts, aligning with the need for active/inactive account status in financial reporting.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"f6e5c3b1-1e6e-4c8e-8b8f-4e1c5e8c8b5e\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"created_date\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadata\": [\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"8427565d6ae7361d577abd8bbd8414e0\",\n          \"column_name\": \"date\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'date' column represents the date of financial transactions, which is relevant for tracking account establishment and supporting financial reporting in GL Accounting.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"f7e5c3b1-1e6e-4c8e-8b8f-4e1c5e8c8b5e\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"modified_date\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadata\": [\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"8427565d6ae7361d577abd8bbd8414e0\",\n          \"column_name\": \"date\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'date' column represents the transaction date in the General Ledger, aligning with the need to track modifications and ensure financial data integrity in the Chart of Accounts.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"business_field_id\": \"f8e5c3b1-1e6e-4c8e-8b8f-4e1c5e8c8b5e\",\n      \"business_field_name\": \"description\",\n      \"description\": \"\",\n      \"field_expression\": \"\",\n      \"mapped_metadata\": [\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"7b7e54c7a58599e3bd2aee95a41e5a46\",\n          \"column_name\": \"account_description\",\n          \"description\": \"The account_description column provides detailed descriptions of accounts, aligning with the need for clarity in financial data organization within GL Accounting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"d594233dfb7e4775de6bb7c326d3818e\",\n          \"column_name\": \"account_type\",\n          \"description\": \"The 'account_type' column categorizes financial accounts, aligning with the need for detailed account descriptions in GL Accounting for effective financial reporting and compliance.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"b752f0a08ba4f281660feb86afaf567b\",\n          \"column_name\": \"account_number\",\n          \"description\": \"The account_number serves as a unique identifier for financial accounts, aligning with the need for clarity and organization in GL Accounting and the Chart of Accounts.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"626ab76092279293c45148d4aef31a6c\",\n          \"column_name\": \"account_number\",\n          \"description\": \"The account_number column serves as a unique identifier for financial accounts, aligning with the need for clarity and organization in financial data management within GL Accounting.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"column_id\": \"37dfea235d8b0fdb4e98aac530a8204f\",\n          \"column_name\": \"dim\",\n          \"description\": \"The column categorizes financial accounts within the hierarchy, aligning with the need for detailed account descriptions in GL Accounting.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"confidence_score\": 0.8848,\n  \"status\": \"active\",\n  \"inferred_by\": \"llm\",\n  \"embedding_input\": \"The 'Chart of Accounts' (Concept ID: ent_chart_of_accounts) is a fundamental entity in GL Accounting that organizes financial data into structured categories, essential for accurate reporting and analysis. This concept encompasses various business fields, including 'account_id', 'account_name', 'account_type', 'parent_account_id', 'account_status', 'created_date', 'modified_date', and 'description', each playing a crucial role in ensuring the integrity and usability of financial data. The validated columns, such as 'account_number' for unique identification, 'account_type' for classification into categories like asset or liability, and 'account_description' for clarity, collectively enhance the organization of financial activities. Additionally, hierarchical relationships are maintained through columns like 'parent_name' and 'dim', which facilitate the classification and reporting of financial accounts, thereby supporting effective financial management and compliance within the organization.\",\n  \"embedding_vector\":[],\n  \"created_at\": {\n    \"$date\": \"2025-12-17T13:25:09.827Z\"\n  },\n  \"updated_at\": {\n    \"$date\": \"2025-12-17T13:25:09.827Z\"\n  }\n}\n```\n"}
